+# ADR-0015 Date of birth on the person
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Status | Proposed |
+| Date | 5 November 2026 |
+| Module | `identity` |
+| Related | ADR-0005 (Drizzle and migrations), ADR-0011 (personal data), TD-06, TD-09 |
+
+## Context
+
+The `identity.person` table has no date of birth. A request asks for an optional date of birth at registration. A date of birth is personal data. ADR-0011 and the personal data check need a purpose, an owner and a retention for each personal column (architecture sections 5 and 9). The Discovery baseline does not name a date of birth or a purpose for it.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Add a nullable column `identity.person.date_of_birth` of type `date`. The migration only adds a column. Old and new app versions can run at the same time (architecture section 5).
+- `registerPerson` accepts an optional `dateOfBirth` as `YYYY-MM-DD`. `getPerson` returns `dateOfBirth`, or `null`.
+- The service rejects a value that is not a real calendar date in the format `YYYY-MM-DD`. It also rejects a date after today in the business time zone, Europe/Berlin (Discovery #102). The error is `InvalidDateOfBirthError`.
+- Column metadata: personal, category `identity`, owner `identity`, retention `account lifetime + 3 years`, the same as the name columns.
+
+## Open points
+
+- **Purpose.** Not confirmed. The column metadata holds a placeholder. The product owner and the privacy owner must give the purpose before this ADR is accepted. Example: age check for a product, or a birthday offer. If no purpose exists, the platform must not collect the date (data minimisation).
+- **Retention.** Confirm that the retention of the name columns also applies here.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A new personal data column. It goes into the record of processing.
+- No event change. `identity.person-registered` does not carry the date of birth.
